NOTE ON LICENSING (not final): MIT is the placeholder license while the
project is young. TheNerdyBox is weighing dual-licensing for this and other
incorporated/rebranded utilities: permissive for individuals and
non-commercial use, with a separate commercial license for anyone earning
from it. Two things to resolve before this note goes away:

1. Whether SignalBox stays permissive (MIT/BSD) or moves to a
   dual-license model.
2. Whether linking against libobs - which OBS itself distributes under
   GPL-2.0-or-later - imposes GPL obligations on the compiled plugin binary
   regardless of the license on this source tree. OBS's own plugin template
   defaults to GPL-2.0-or-later for exactly this reason; a number of
   community plugins ship MIT/BSD anyway on the theory that a runtime-loaded
   module isn't "linking" in the FSF sense. This project has not taken a
   position on that theory yet - see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

Until resolved, treat MIT as the intent for TheNerdyBox's own original code
in src/ and data/, not as a settled legal conclusion about the distributed
binary.
